From 83da80703631800b77e7138f9188db47629282ba Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Sat, 30 May 2026 07:14:30 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] freedreno/a2xx: A22X per-tile drain use legacy KGSL
 pattern (CACHE_FLUSH + WAIT_REG_EQ(RBBM_DEBUG bit24))

prepare_tile_fini_ib() previously used a plain OUT_WFI between the per-tile
draws and the EDRAM_COPY resolve, sufficient to ensure the mode-transition
COLOR_DEPTH <-> EDRAM_COPY is on an idle pipeline. On A220 a plain WFI does
not wait for VGT DMA, so a tile's draws can leak past the resolve and write
stale data.

CACHE_FLUSH_TS + WFI works (heavier path; needs a scratch buffer for the
timestamp), but the production legacy KGSL driver -- which renders the same
heavy multi-bin scenes on the same A220 silicon without ever wedging --
uses a lighter pattern at the same boundary:

  CACHE_FLUSH                    (plain event, no _TS)
  WAIT_REG_EQ(0x39b mask=1<<24 val=1<<24)

Bit 24 of REG_A2XX_RBBM_DEBUG is a vendor opaque cache-flush+EDRAM-
coherency completion bit (see the per-draw pattern in fd2_draw.c::
emit_cacheflush for the same construct).

Consolidates 0018 + 0032 from the previous patch series (drops the
unused scratch_buf+seqno path).

Upstream-Status: Pending

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a2xx/fd2_gmem.c | 24 +++++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 19 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a2xx/fd2_gmem.c b/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a2xx/fd2_gmem.c
index cfd2af48dbc..e2a74bd14cc 100644
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a2xx/fd2_gmem.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a2xx/fd2_gmem.c
@@ -182,11 +182,25 @@ prepare_tile_fini_ib(struct fd_batch *batch) assert_dt
    OUT_RING(ring, fui((float)gmem->bin_h / 2.0f)); /* YSCALE */
    OUT_RING(ring, fui((float)gmem->bin_h / 2.0f)); /* YOFFSET */
 
-   /* A22X: WFI before changing RB_MODECONTROL to ensure pipeline is idle.
-    * Mode transitions between COLOR_DEPTH and EDRAM_COPY require sync.
-    */
-   if (!is_a20x(ctx->screen))
-      OUT_WFI(ring);
+   /* A22X: per-tile drain before the EDRAM_COPY resolve, using the legacy
+    * KGSL pattern -- plain CACHE_FLUSH event + WAIT_REG_EQ on RBBM_DEBUG
+    * (0x39b) bit 24. The tile's draws must have fully landed in GMEM before
+    * the resolve reads it back, and the mode transition COLOR_DEPTH <->
+    * EDRAM_COPY also needs sync. Plain OUT_WFI is insufficient on A220 (it
+    * does not wait for VGT DMA); CACHE_FLUSH_TS + WFI works but is heavier
+    * than what KGSL emits and equivalent in coverage. RBBM_DEBUG bit 24 is
+    * a vendor opaque cache-flush+EDRAM-coherency completion bit (see
+    * fd2_draw.c::emit_cacheflush comment for the per-draw pattern). */
+   if (!is_a20x(ctx->screen)) {
+      OUT_PKT3(ring, CP_EVENT_WRITE, 1);
+      OUT_RING(ring, CACHE_FLUSH);
+
+      OUT_PKT3(ring, CP_WAIT_REG_EQ, 4);
+      OUT_RING(ring, REG_A2XX_RBBM_DEBUG);  /* 0x39b */
+      OUT_RING(ring, 1u << 24);             /* expected: bit 24 set */
+      OUT_RING(ring, 1u << 24);             /* mask: only check bit 24 */
+      OUT_RING(ring, 1);                    /* 1 poll/iter */
+   }
 
    OUT_PKT3(ring, CP_SET_CONSTANT, 2);
    OUT_RING(ring, CP_REG(REG_A2XX_RB_MODECONTROL));
-- 
